amfX2C (h4 + atom-block-diagonal G_L): one negative-energy state rises
through the gap; at k=5 it sits at the F 1s energy (-27.51) and the F 1s
state is assigned to the negative-energy half, so X and the 2c Hamiltonian
collapse.  x2cmp (molecular G[D_atoms]) and X2C-1e keep the gap at -2c^2.
